{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Management-fee revenue belongs to the platform adviser under its advisory agreement with the fund. The adviser pays ordinary operating expenses from that revenue, except expenses the sponsor has contractually agreed to assume under the unitary-fee arrangement. The sponsor’s payment obligation is limited to the fee remainder and the contract’s covered expenses; it does not change the fund’s fee or imply a standard percentage split.\n\nThe fund’s continuing obligation is to pay the advisory fee to the adviser under the fund’s advisory agreement. The adviser remains responsible to the fund for its advisory services and for any fund expenses not covered by the unitary-fee or sponsor agreement."}}
